dangling plot threads and dumb decisions  Avatar the way of water is gorgeous epic  and moving but these plot holes prove it  isn't perfect  after the return of Colonel quarrich  Jake and his family decide to go into  hiding to protect the omotakaya clan  from the Colonel's wrath since the  colonel only wants revenge on his human  form's killer Jake assumes quarridge  will leave the omotakaya alone but going  into hiding doesn't guarantee anything  the plan hinges on the assumption that  quarrych knows what Jake knows Jake  didn't exactly announce to the resource  development Administration aka the RDA  that he'd be leaving the jungle quarrich  has no reason to believe Jake and his  family would leave their home in the  Hallelujah mountains where they'd be  mostly safe thanks to the flux vortex in  the omitakaya's guerrilla warfare  tactics it follows that he would try to  find Jake in the Hallelujah mountains  first even if korich couldn't seize the  Hallelujah mountains he would certainly  be capable of taking individual Navi  prisoners like he already did with  spider and almost stood with Jake's  children if the omotakaya tried to  explain that Jake fled quarch might not  believe them after all he didn't believe  the innocent metcaina tribes when they  told him they hadn't seen Jake and he  still torched their homes it was only by  a Stroke of Luck that the omitakaya  tribe was spared to the same fate Jake  has a huge bounty on his head in the way  of water but the plot may be overstating  his importance does the RDA really think  that taking out a single person will  silence the navi Insurrection for good  it makes sense for quarch to be  single-mindedly focused on finding Jake  he doesn't care about the other Navi he  just wants revenge but kwarich isn't the  only one making decisions at the RDA  certainly killing Jake would deal a huge  blow to the resistance he was the one  who rallied the navi to Victory 15 years  ago and without him it would take them a  long time to regroup Jake is also one of  the few characters on Pandora who has  inside knowledge of the RDA but he's not  the only one who knows how to use human  technology and he's not the only one  capable of organizing an army this  oversight is especially apparent in the  battle at Sea viewers will notice that  tonawari gathers his clan into an  imposing battle formation and on very  short notice too this moment reminds  audiences that the navi are quite  capable of organizing themselves clearly  the movement to free Pandora will live  on even if Jake died so maybe the last  thing the RDA wants is to turn Jake into  a martyr when they learn that their kids  are being held hostage in the forest  Jake Anthony teary swoop and to rescue  them it's a good thing that they're able  to respond so quickly but it's a little  surprising that their rescue party  consists of only two people why didn't  they ask their clan for reinforcements  perhaps with backup they could have  prevented spiders capture you'd think  Jake Anthony teary would pull out all  the stops to save their children Jake  and his son were both equipped with  throat mics so it should have been  relatively easy for Jake to radio for  help after all it's not like Jake and  his family are the only Navi using human  technology considering that Jake and the  omitakaya clan have been staging  guerrilla warfare against the RDA for  the past year it's hard to believe that  all the navi aren't equipped with throat  mics while there may not be an in-story  reason for this the choice at least  makes sense from a storytelling  perspective most likely the filmmakers  wanted to keep the cast to a manageable  size and that meant not dragging a bunch  of additional characters into the fight  the film is about Jake and his family so  it makes sense that only these  characters would be involved if nothing  else this is one movie Epic in scale but  maintaining an intimate Focus is still  no doubt some viewers were frustrated  watching the scene knowing that Jake  could have made a smarter move  without unobtainium the events of Avatar  would have never happened after all it  was the whole reason the RDA funded the  mission on Pandora there's this little  gray rock sells for 20 million a kilo  that's the only reason yet unobtainium  seems to be the last thing on the rda's  Mind these days General Ardmore insists  that the company's new objective is  colonization not mining because Earth is  pretty much a lost cause at this point  it's understandable why the rda's  priorities might have changed 15 years  have passed on Earth more than enough  time for war and climate change to  render it nearly unlivable perhaps all  the unobtainium in the world won't do  them any good because soon everyone on  the planet is going to need to jump ship  still it's a little strange that the  film never mentions unobtanium not even  once he would think that the miraculous  material would come in handy for the RDA  if they want to expand their colony and  crush the navi resistance the rda's  purpose is further obfuscated in the  scene where tolkun Hunter makes scoresby  extracts a chemical called Amrita from  the toku's brain scoresby brags that  Amrita can effectively stop aging  entirely making it Eclipse unobtainium  as the most valuable resource on Pandora  he also adds that Amrita is paying for  everything on Pandora which seems to  contradict the notion that the RDA cares  only about colonization while it makes  sense that Amrita is extremely valuable  it seems doubtful it would be of much  use to the humans back on a dying planet  Earth  Colonel quarrich goes to some Great  Lengths to bait Jake and capture his  children even though he already has one  of Jake's children in his custody okay  spider is technically Jake's adoptive  son but Jake still cares about the boy  why lay out an elaborate trap for Jake  when the RDA already has something Jake  wants obviously the real reason quartz  doesn't hold spider hostage is clear  spider is his son and as one key scene  from the climax demonstrates quarch  loves his son more than he hates Jake  I'm getting all emotional I might just  give you a big wet kiss yet once again  quarrych isn't the one in charge and it  seems like General Ardmore has no such  qualms about using spider that way why  doesn't she just order kwarich to Ransom  his son the only reason why the RDA  might not take advantage of the prisoner  they already had would be if quorge was  convinced that spider was genuinely  cooperating with his captors but General  Ardmore would need to be convinced too  and somehow it seems doubtful she would  automatically trust the boy like kwarich  Avatar the way of water isn't the first  movie in the Avatar franchise to  contradict itself about the science of  Pandora the first film made it clear  that humans couldn't survive long  without a mask in Pandora's atmosphere  specifically they'd be unconscious after  20 seconds and dead after 4 minutes but  that doesn't seem to stop courage from  opening an airlock and then firing on  Jake for a heck of a lot longer than 20  seconds though granted he's basically a  finely tuned murder machine and would  have no trouble holding his breath that  long  but the sequel also plays a little fast  and loose with the specifics early in  the movie spider establishes a key rule  of World building he tells the navi you  can breathe earth air for hours I can  only breathe yours for like 10 seconds  yet quarrich who now inhabits a navi  Avatar with recombinant DNA recom for  short doesn't seem to follow this rule  quarrich is quite comfortable breathing  Pandora's air as well as the earth air  inside the RDA compound aside from a  brief moment when quarge sucks in a few  gulps from a gas mask before talking to  spider one possible explanation here is  that the recoms were bred to be able to  breathe in both Earth's atmosphere and  that of Pandora though it might have  been nice if the film had taken a moment  to mention that just breathe  breathe to be honest courage attempting  to ride a Banshee wasn't the smartest  move surely kwarriage could tell that  spider was hoping the colonel would  humiliate himself however that's not a  plot hole in itself because it makes  perfect sense for quarrych's character  he's stubborn and wants to prove he can  do anything that Jake can do so that's  why he takes the bait however one moment  from the Banshee scene doesn't quite add  up quarrych has seen tumbling off the  cliff on the back of a banshee much like  Jake did in the first film only to  emerge Victorious a minute later how  does he learn so quickly clearly the  colonel is a novice to Banshee writing  not even knowing that he should muzzle  the Banshee before trying to mount it  according to the rules established in  the first movie quarridge could have  only tamed the Beast by completing the  bond which involves linking the nerve  receptors in his cue to the Banshees  receptors but how does quarridge know  about this most likely the RDA knows  about this Ritual from Jake's video logs  from the first movie but whether or not  quarch knows is a different story  knowing quarrych he wouldn't do his  homework he has a pretty rudimentary  grasp of the navi language to the point  that spider says he has the vocabulary  of a three-year-old these Avatar movies  sure do have a grudge against babies  you're like a baby  anyway the point is the colonel would  have probably only researched the bare  minimum necessary for the mission and  unless he predicted that his guide would  goad him into trying to tame a Banshee  the bonding ritual probably wasn't in  his plans  the first half of the way of water seems  to be building toward quarrich and his  fellow recoms trying to go undercover  among the navi that's why they go out of  their way to tame banshees and learn the  language so they can get close enough to  Jake to kill him and then destroy the  navi Insurrection from the inside yet  this plot thread is abandoned halfway  through the movie it's understandable  why the filmmakers didn't take this  route the undercover angle was already  explored in the first movie with Jake  and honestly the recoms wouldn't have  gotten very far they wouldn't fool a  real navi for an instant however the way  that kwarich and his team switch gears  is a little contrived the RDA  conveniently picks up a signal from a  rogue gunship which sends the plot in a  New Direction everything that happens in  the second half of the movie hinges on  quarge guessing correctly that the  unidentified aircraft will lead him  straight to Jake that's an awfully lucky  guess up until this point quarrette had  every reason to believe that Jake was in  the Hallelujah mountains besides it  feels implausible that General Ardmore  would let quarrych travel Halfway Around  Pandora on a hunch there's one plot hole  in avatar The Way of water so annoy  enormous that Reddit users called it out  almost immediately after the film came  out where is Jake's Army when he needs  it most the Met kaina Clan had Jake's  back throughout the first hostage  exchange on the ship and the ensuing  battle but the moment that the chief's  daughter Soraya is rescued the clan is  nowhere to be found leaving Jake and his  family to fend for themselves so why did  they bail perhaps the Met kaina  retreated after Soraya was safe because  they no longer had a personal stake in  the conflict or maybe they were  physically unable to help one Reddit  user speculated they couldn't get past  the fire on the water that is a fair  point though it seems like the mech  hyena might have been able to swim under  meanwhile another redditor offered a  solid explanation even if it wasn't an  in-universe explanation saying that the  real focus of this part was the family  unit had the filmmakers included the  whole Army in the final battle it would  have become too crowded trying to focus  on any characters other than Jake and  his family would honestly have only  heard the story  [Music]  foreign
 

